<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Parallel Cross Sections</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Polylines &gt; Cross Sections &gt; Parallel</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Parallel Cross Sections</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command creates a number of parallel cross sections through the visible selection. The direction in which the cutting planes will lie and the spacing between them is also defined by user. You can use points from scan data and meshes only. All polylines created by this method will be placed in separate groups (</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>X Section</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Y Section</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Z Section</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">) depending on what direction they were extracted.</span></p>
<p><span class="Command">Parallel Cross Sections</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command is grayed if there are no scan data or mesh selections or all selections are hidden. It works on wholly selected entities as well as on partial selections. In case of partial selection only those parts of polylines are extracted that are within the selection although the parameters are calculated for all objects with selections.&#160;</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="Images/parallel_cross_section.gif" width="220px" height="528px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Cross sections</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Number of polylines</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– number of sections. This number is not always the same with the number of generated polylines – if there is a gap crossing the section, two polylines are created. This parameter is calculated automatically and is based on the spacing.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Width</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– section width. This parameter is calculated automatically and is based on the size of the object in the corresponding direction from the current view.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Spacing</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– distance between sections. Default value is 10mm.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Starting parameters</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Starting point</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>X</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Y</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Z</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– pick a point from the screen or type-in the co-ordinates of the starting point of the sectioning. These parameters are calculated automatically and are based on the parameters from Cross section group and current orientation of the viewport.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Plane normal</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>X</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Y</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Z</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– pick a line/normal/axis from the screen or type-in the normal of the plane where the starting section lays. These parameters are calculated automatically and are based on the parameters from Cross section group and current orientation of the viewport.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Extract parameters</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Tolerancing</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– chordal tolerance. This is the maximum error tolerance for polyline deviation from the original profile of the data. See</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="chordal_tolerancing.htm">Chordal Tolerancing</a></span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">for details. Default value is 0.001mm.&#160;</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Weld</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– distance below which sections will be welded together. This will form continuous sections, for example, on patch boundaries where the scan data does not overlap perfectly. Default value is 0.1mm.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Align</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Reference</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;">– select a reference object for aligning (viewport, world, plane, or plane reducible entity). Then use</span> <span lang="EN-GB">X</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB">Y</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;">, or</span> <span lang="EN-GB">Z</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;">buttons to choose the direction. For datum entities</span> <span lang="EN-GB">Z</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;">button always defines section plane parallel to the plane where the entity lie.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight:bold;" class="kadov-p-CImportant">
<p class="Important"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;">If a datum entity is selected as reference it should be close to the object from, which parallel polylines will be extracted. In this case the extraction extents are defined by the datum.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Direction</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>X</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– X-axis along which the parallel polylines will be aligned.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP222709827" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-left:8px;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image056.jpg" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Y</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– Y-axis along which the parallel polylines will be aligned.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP234945559" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-left:8px;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image058.jpg" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Z</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– Z-axis along which the parallel polylines will be aligned.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP171517769" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-left:8px;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image060.jpg" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<p class="whs7"><span lang="EN-GB">See</span> Scroll Bars <span lang="EN-GB">for explanation of the viewport axes.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Buttons</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Extract</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– extracts the polylines as separate entities according to the current axis and settings.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Close</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– closes this dialog.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">You may freely rotate, pan, and zoom the viewport while ‘Cross Section - Parallel’ dialog is open. You may also change the selection, delete, and perform other visualisation commands.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">After extracting polylines in all three directions you will get the <a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a5" style="text-decoration:underline;">following polylines</a>:</span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP234934047" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image064.jpg" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Each polyline section has the same colour as its original mesh. If you have more than two meshes with different colours, then their correspondent polylines can be easily recognised. Anyway, if you have more than one polyline section on a single mesh, you may paint each section in different colour in order to distinguish them.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a4" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP290052596" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-left:8px;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image066.jpg" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">See</span> Tree Context Menus <span lang="EN-GB">from Visualisation chapter of Common for details.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span class="Command">Parallel Cross Sections</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to create sections from point data for export to a CAD or other computer system. This sectioning is the most commonly used.</span></p>
